From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 16:29:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 494/496] [DS4.1] No kernel-family switch:
 VLLM_DS41_KERNEL_BACKEND goes

VLLM_DS41_KERNEL_BACKEND defaulted to b12x and serving set it to tilelang.
With the B12X family gone from the model, every engine conditional on it
collapses to its TileLang branch:

- envs.py: the variable goes, and VLLM_DS41_ATTENTION_COMPUTE, whose only
  reader was the B12X sparse MLA;
- DeepseekV41ForCausalLMConfig: the TILELANG attention backend and the tilelang
  linear and MoE backends, an explicit other backend fails as before; it also
  sets the new SchedulerConfig.align_prefill_chunks;
- scheduler: aligned prefill chunks are that flag (the module constant read
  the variable), so they stay DeepSeek V4.1's as under serving's setting, and
  the CED skip policy reads the same flag;
- CudaCommunicator: tensor-parallel groups always build sparknet's one-shot
  collectives (a single-node group skips them, as sparknet decides) with the
  rank-order all-reduce past the one-shot limit, rank-order reduce-scatter,
  one-shot broadcast and the TileLang shard concat; VLLM_ENABLE_ROCE_ALLREDUCE,
  which selected B12X's RoCE collectives, is refused; b12x_roce_all_reduce.py
  goes (nothing else in vLLM imports it), with PyNCCL's all-reduce past the
  one-shot limit that only that policy used, and its two size variables
  (VLLM_ROCE_ALLREDUCE_MAX_SIZE, VLLM_ROCE_ALLGATHER_MAX_SIZE);
- gpu_worker: the TileLang preparation and startup progress always run;
- comments and docstrings that named the variable.

Tests: the RoCE policy's broadcast tests are the one-shot all-gather's (the
B12X policy's PyNCCL broadcast goes); the config, CED skip-policy, aligned
chunk and kernel-preparation tests run without the variable.
